  <Dialog id="surface-dialog" title="Surface anatomy"><p class="dialog-lead">Three layers. One clear reading surface.</p><ol class="anatomy-list"><li><strong>01 / Pigment</strong><p>Decorative strokes sit behind the card. Stable masks keep their edges and bristle tracks consistent.</p><code>--ac-pigment / --ac-pigment-2</code></li><li><strong>02 / Dry ground</strong><p>An opaque surface separates the text from any changing color beneath it.</p><code>--ac-surface / --ac-ink</code></li><li><strong>03 / Action</strong><p>A paired action and label color, a 44px minimum target, and a visible focus ring make the control usable.</p><code>--ac-accent / --ac-on-accent / --ac-focus</code></li></ol><p class="small-note">This is a native dialog: Tab stays inside, Escape closes it, and focus returns to the trigger.</p></Dialog>
